# Worker Dockerfile Patterns

## Base Image

Always use `python:3.11-slim`:

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim
```

## System Dependencies

Install PostgreSQL client libraries:

```dockerfile
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    gcc \
    g++ \
    libpq-dev \
    curl \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
```

## UV Installation

Install `uv` for fast package management:

```dockerfile
RUN curl -LsSf https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/latest/download/uv-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz | \
    tar -xz -C /tmp && \
    find /tmp -name "uv" -type f -executable -exec mv {} /usr/local/bin/uv \; && \
    chmod +x /usr/local/bin/uv && \
    rm -rf /tmp/uv* && \
    uv --version
```

## Dependency Installation

**Extract dependencies from pyproject.toml and install (NO editable install):**

```dockerfile
COPY worker/pyproject.toml /app/pyproject.toml
COPY worker /app/worker
COPY backend/config /app/config

RUN cd /app && python -c "import tomllib; f=open('pyproject.toml','rb'); d=tomllib.load(f); deps=d['project']['dependencies']; import subprocess; subprocess.run(['uv', 'pip', 'install', '--system', '--no-cache'] + deps, check=True)"
```

## Important Notes

- **Never use `-e .` (editable install)** - install dependencies only
- Copy `pyproject.toml` before source code for better caching
- Mount `backend/config` for access to `tags.csv` if needed
- Use `--system --no-cache` flags with `uv pip install`

## Run Command

```dockerfile
CMD ["python", "-m", "worker.src.main"]
```

## Health Check

```dockerfile
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --retries=3 --start-period=60s \
    CMD python -c "import sys; sys.exit(0)" || exit 1
```
